        <title type="html"><![CDATA[SharedArrayBuffer and Atomic - remove interactive examples]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43060</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43060"/>
        <updated>2026-02-09T06:35:46.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">The interactive examples in <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Atomics" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">Atomics</code></a> and  <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/SharedArrayBuffer" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">SharedArrayBuffer</code></a> don't work, because they depend on (and make sense for) <code class="notranslate">SharedArrayBuffer</code> and that has security concerns that mean you can't run the examples in an interactive example, or even copy them into the console.<br>
The Rari team say that the <a href="https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/971#issuecomment-3750043131" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/fred/issues/971/hovercard">interactive examples infrastructure will not be fixed</a>, so this PR attempts to remove the examples in a sensible way.</p>
<p dir="auto">Specifically I have added note about  the security concerns between the Examples and first example in all cases:</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">Note that these examples cannot be run directly from the console or an arbitrary web page, because <code class="notranslate">SharedArrayBuffer</code> is not defined unless its <a href="/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/SharedArrayBuffer#security_requirements">security requirements</a> are met.</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">I have removed the interactive examples. However IMO these are better than the examples in that they have a little more documentation alongside explaining what is going on. So where sensible, I have copied information or patterns from the interactive example into the first example in the body.</p>
<p dir="auto">Lastly, have fixed up a spurious line endings in the first commit.</p>]]></content>
